## Conversation
The user asked for a minimal DFlash2 implementation with tests and a draft pull request. Final read-only reviews found that serving artifact failures could deadlock distributed ranks and that DP rank zero was not unique under sequence parallelism.

## Actions
Synchronized primary and fallback save errors through the global Gloo group before any rank returns or raises. Moved directory creation and artifact writes onto global rank zero. Preserved the replicated fallback and the FULL_SHARD fail-fast guard. Strengthened grouped-convolution and selector tests, and added a two-rank control-flow regression for a global non-writer whose DP rank is zero. Replaced repeated whole-sys.modules import stubs with one targeted loader. Ran the four isolated export tests, 20 focused tests with 14 subtests, 109 related tests with 14 subtests, Ruff, formatting, pre-commit, and diff checks.

## Errors & Mistakes
The first combined related-suite run failed because a string-based mock patched a different cached trainer module than the inherited method used. The failure was: RuntimeError: Gloo group has not been initialized. Call _init_gloo_group() first. The test now patches the inherited method's globals. A later isolated export-class run exposed repeated whole-sys.modules restoration as ArrowKeyError: A type extension with name datasets.features.features.Array2DExtensionType already defined. The targeted loader restores only the two Mooncake entries and keeps transitive imports registered.

## Dead Ends
Keeping the final barrier did not solve rank-zero write failures because the writer could raise before reaching it. Selecting the writer by dp_rank also failed under sequence parallelism because more than one global rank can have DP rank zero.

## Hints for Future Agents
Serving artifact writes must use cache_rank, which is the global rank, rather than dp_rank. All ranks must participate in error synchronization before any rank raises. Do not restore a local model.state_dict fallback for FULL_SHARD because it can contain rank-local DTensor shards.

## Codebase Discoveries
TrainerActor initializes a global Gloo group before it constructs a trainer. Trainer.cache_rank records the global rank, while Trainer.dp_rank can be a subgroup rank under USP. StateDictOptions with full_state_dict and cpu_offload returns the complete state on global rank zero.

## Open Questions
The final code was not exercised in a real multi-rank GPU or SGLang training run. The regression covers the distributed control flow with simulated ranks.
